## Release (Boss only)

0. Before merging ANY branch: merge the main branch into it (or squash it onto a fresh main in a worktree on disk,
   never in `/tmp`) and rerun everything on the result, as one command: `<for example: crew publish ...>`. Install,
   migrate on a scratch database only, typecheck, lint, the full tests. Stop on a conflict or a failure. The same run
   bumps the version (`publish.version`, README "Publish"), so no branch does. This is the merger's job (Boss), not the
   workers': things go stale in unexpected ways fast.
1. Back up the database: `<command>`
